                        "entry_id": "a450a7e6-d805-3cf3-914a-e39594c7205b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To knock (a person) over by striking them across the neck or upper body with an outstretched arm, mimicking the motion of running into a low clothesline."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Canada",
                            "US",
                            "informal",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "34ad97e8-926d-4e01-9eb2-f2ed32d40800",
                                "sense_id": "7896259e-be3b-32ee-9be4-f28f51e6ba6e",
                                "text": "The referee called a personal foul, when he clotheslined the running back."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b80b8cb-6b06-45f0-9253-a995321a324d",
                                "sense_id": "7896259e-be3b-32ee-9be4-f28f51e6ba6e",
                                "text": "One beast jams out its arm, as if to clothesline me, jagged claws poised to take my head off at the neck. I let my feet fall from under me, throwing my legs forward, praying for some momentum, ducking and sliding, a mad limbo to freedom."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddc211c5-d339-4deb-adb1-e003555fd838",
                                "sense_id": "7896259e-be3b-32ee-9be4-f28f51e6ba6e",
                                "text": "\"I turned around and the next thing I was taken out by this big guy. I'm not sure if he punched me or clothes-lined me,\" he said."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
